<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);Nullable</WarningsAsErrors>

    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>

    <Authors>Haik Asatryan</Authors>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/HaikAsatryan/ResultCrafter</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/HaikAsatryan/ResultCrafter</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>

    <PackageIcon>resultcrafter-icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>

    <Version>3.0.0</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>BREAKING: targets net10.0 only (runs on .NET 10 and later, tested on .NET 10 and .NET 11); Error is now a sealed class (error.Type, not error.Value.Type); SuccessKind.None is the default and failures carry it; default(Result&lt;T&gt;) and default(Result) now throw from IsSuccess, Map, Match and every To*Result instead of reporting success; Result.AcceptedLocation is renamed Location; Error.BadRequest takes IReadOnlyDictionary; a Result, Result&lt;T&gt; or Error returned from an endpoint without mapping now throws instead of going out as 200; EF Core 40001/40P01 (serialization failure, deadlock) now reach the 500 handler instead of 409; ToProblemResult() and the void Result controller methods return ActionResult; ResultCrafterLogger and ProblemDetailsEnricher are internal; ResultCrafter.MediatR is discontinued. Fixed: error responses keep the house shape whatever the order of AddControllers() and AddResultCrafter() and whatever the Accept header; WithValidation skips validation after a parameter binding failure; AddResultCrafterValidation registers internal validators; the 500 handler honors ExceptionHandlerOptions.StatusCodeSelector; .NET 11 unreadable JSON bodies and built-in AddValidation() responses get the house BadRequest shape with JSON field keys. Added: typed Error.With() overloads for extra ProblemDetails members (NativeAOT-safe), Error.TooManyRequests(retryAfter) with the Retry-After header, the ProblemResponse OpenAPI schema on all Produces* helpers, and a NativeAOT smoke test in CI. Upgrading from 2.x: https://github.com/HaikAsatryan/ResultCrafter/blob/main/docs/migrating-to-3.md</PackageReleaseNotes>

    <!-- Build quality -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

    <!-- Source/symbols -->
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Each package packs the README next to its csproj: nuget.org shows raw HTML as text and blanks relative links,
       so the GitHub README at the root cannot be reused there. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(IsPackable)' == 'true'">
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)assets/resultcrafter-icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
    <None Include="$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
